{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-101831-r4615163","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Dirty Rice","sourcePageId":101831,"sourceRevision":"4615163","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:28:52Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Dirty%20Rice&oldid=4615163","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:41:38.871Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Louisiana recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using bay leaf","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using celery","Category:Recipes using chicken gizzard","Category:Recipes using chicken liver","Category:Recipes using cumin","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using green bell pepper","Category:Recipes using liver","Category:Recipes using mustard powder","Category:Recipes using pork broth and stock","Category:Recipes using rice","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Side dish recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"44ef89aa4a2ab74c8bffa605443ba3ff52215ab94ace4d98662d1264bdda3b16","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Rice recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cajun cuisine|Cajun cuisine]]\n\n'''Dirty rice''' is a traditional [[cookbook:Cajun cuisine|Cajun]] dish made from white rice cooked with small pieces of chicken liver or giblets, which give it a dark (\"dirty\") color.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Schmaltz|chicken fat]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]] (225 g) chicken [[Cookbook:Chicken#Other|gizzards]] (optional)  \n* 2 teaspoons [[cookbook:paprika|paprika]]\n* ¼ lb (110 g) [[cookbook:pork|pork]], ground\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Mustard|dry mustard]]  \n* 1 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaf]]  \n* 1 teaspoon [[cookbook:cumin|cumin]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Onion|yellow onion]]\n* ½ teaspoon [[cookbook:thyme|thyme]] \n* 1½ stalks [[cookbook:celery|celery]] \n* ½ teaspoon [[cookbook:oregano|oregano]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Each|ea]]. green [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell pepper]]  \n* 2 tablespoons [[cookbook:butter|butter]] \n* 1 [[cookbook:garlic|garlic]] clove  \n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Stock|pork stock]] \n* 1 teaspoon [[cookbook:Tabasco Sauce|Tabasco sauce]] \n* ½ lb (225 g) [[Cookbook:Liver|chicken livers]] (optional)  \n* 1 teaspoon [[cookbook:salt|salt]]  \n* 1 cup cooked [[cookbook:rice|rice]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# [[cookbook:Mincing|Mince]] onion, bell pepper, celery and garlic. \n# [[cookbook:Purée|Grind]] livers and gizzards. \n# Place fat, gizzards, pork and bay leaves in large heavy [[cookbook:skillet|skillet]] over high heat; cook until meat is thoroughly [[Cookbook:Brown|browned]], about 6 minutes, stirring occasionally. \n# [[Cookbook:Stirring|Stir]] in the onion, celery, bell pepper, garlic, Tabasco, salt, pepper, paprika, mustard, cumin, thyme, and oregano; stir thoroughly, scraping pan bottom well. \n# Add the butter and stir until melted.\n# Reduce heat to medium and cook about 8 minutes, stirring constantly and scraping pan bottom well. \n# Add the stock or water and stir until any mixture sticking to the pan bottom comes loose; cook about 8 minutes over high heat, stirring once. \n# Stir in the chicken livers and cook about 2 minutes.\n# Add the rice and stir thoroughly; cover pan and turn heat to very low; cook about 5 minutes. \n# Remove from heat and leave covered until rice is tender, about 10 minutes. \n# Remove bay leaves and serve immediately.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken gizzard]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken liver]]\n[[Category:Recipes using liver]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Louisiana recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bay leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pork broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard powder]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Dirty Rice","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 tablespoons chicken fat","sourceText":"2 tablespoons chicken fat","amountText":"2 tablespoons chicken fat","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 teaspoon black pepper","sourceText":"1 teaspoon black pepper","amountText":"1 teaspoon black pepper","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"½ lb (225 g) chicken gizzards (optional)","sourceText":"½ lb (225 g) chicken gizzards (optional)","amountText":"½ lb (225 g) chicken gizzards (optional)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 teaspoons paprika","sourceText":"2 teaspoons paprika","amountText":"2 teaspoons paprika","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"¼ lb (110 g) pork, ground","sourceText":"¼ lb (110 g) pork, ground","amountText":"¼ lb (110 g) pork, ground